{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "g-styles",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Style library (copy a card onto any canvas)",
			"x": -40,
			"y": 180,
			"width": 2640,
			"height": 1000,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "readme",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "# Assets\nMake game art with AI, right here. Each **recipe card** makes one asset.\n\n**Right-click a recipe card:**\n- **Generate \"name\" now** runs it.\n- **Preview request (free)** shows what would be sent.\n- **Redo finish only (free)** redoes the crunch from the saved original.\n- **Status: idea / go** sets it to wait or to run.\n\nThe card turns **yellow** while running, **green** when done, **red** on an error. The result appears as small cards to the right, and in `assets/generated/`. Animations also get an **MP4** and pictures a **JPG**, for sharing in apps that do not show WebP.\n\n**Kinds of card** (the second line):\n- `image`: a new picture from a prompt.\n- `edit`: changes the picture that points to it (arrows labelled `image 1`, `image 2` when there are two).\n- `animate`: a short video from the picture that points to it, kept as a few held frames like a 90s CD-ROM game.\n- `cutout`: free. Keys a picture (or every frame of an animation) off its green screen.\n- `composite`: free. Pastes an `actor` on a green screen into a `room`.\n- `style`: adds its prompt words (`template`) and crunch to every card it points to.\n\n**Where art lives now:** each character, screen, and item has its own canvas in its own folder, and its art saves beside it, in `art/`:\n- [[Arthur.canvas]] (characters/arthur)\n- [[south-gate.canvas]] (screens/south-gate)\n- [[guard-tower-04.canvas]] (screens/guard-tower-04)\n- [[contractor-id.canvas]] (items/contractor-id)\n\nThis canvas keeps the guide, the model list, and the **style library** below. To use a style on another canvas, copy its card there and draw an arrow from it. Recipes made here save into `assets/generated/`.\n\n`Cmd+P` \u2192 *Game Tools* also has: generate every card set to go, watch this canvas, play the game, and open the workbench.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": -1100,
			"width": 1100,
			"height": 760
		},
		{
			"id": "models",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Models (checked 1 Oct 2026)\n| model: | What | Cost |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `z-image` | Z-Image Turbo: rooms and backgrounds | $0.005 / MP |\n| `krea-2` | Krea 2 Turbo: actors and props on green | $0.008 / MP |\n| `qwen-edit` | Qwen Image Edit 2511: change part of a picture | about $0.024 |\n| `flux2-edit` | FLUX.2 edit | \u2014 |\n| `h3-max-turbo` | MiniMax H3 Max Turbo, image to video | $0.025 / s (480p) |\n| `minimax-h3` | MiniMax H3, image to video, first + last frame | \u2014 |\n| `flux-lora`, `flux-2-lora` | FLUX with a LoRA (not used now) | \u2014 |\n\nAny other fal model: set `endpoint:` and `params:`.",
			"x": 1200,
			"y": -1100,
			"width": 900,
			"height": 600,
			"color": "3"
		},
		{
			"id": "style-room",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## fmv-room\nstyle\n# Pre-rendered 1990s CG rooms. Use with model: z-image.\nprefix: A still frame from a 1995 CD-ROM computer game, a pre-rendered 3D CGI background, early 1990s 3D rendering with flat shading, low-polygon models and simple textures\nsuffix: no people, no text or lettering",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 260,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 260,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "style-actor-green",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## fmv-actor-green\nstyle\n# Live actors on a green screen, to key out. Use with model: krea-2.\n# Keep green out of the wardrobe.\nprefix: A 1995 video capture of a live-action actor filmed for a CD-ROM game on a chroma-key stage\nsuffix: standing in front of a solid bright chroma-key green screen, solid pure green #00FF00 background, evenly lit",
			"x": 640,
			"y": 260,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 300,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "arthur-keep",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## arthur-keep\nstyle\n# Holds Arthur steady in edits: only the named part changes.\ntemplate: \"Keep the exact same man: same face, grey slicked-back hair and grey mustache, same black security uniform shirt with epaulettes and silver badge, holding the same handheld intercom handset. Keep the exact same framing, crop, camera position and waist-up pose, and the same flat, evenly lit chroma-key green screen background, lighting and camera quality. Only change {prompt}\"\n",
			"x": 1280,
			"y": 260,
			"width": 560,
			"height": 360,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "talk-loop",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## talk-loop\nstyle\n# For mood talking loops: keep the mood, keep the green screen still.\ntemplate: \"The night guard {prompt}, keeping exactly the same expression and mood, small natural mouth and head movements, locked-off static camera, the green screen background stays flat, evenly lit and unchanged\"\n",
			"x": 1920,
			"y": 260,
			"width": 560,
			"height": 320,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "fmv-prop-green",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## fmv-prop-green\nstyle\n# Props to cut out and layer over a scene: flat, front-on, on pure green.\ntemplate: \"A 1995 pre-rendered 3D CGI game asset, early 1990s 3D rendering with flat shading, low-polygon model and simple textures, seen straight on in a front orthographic view: {prompt}. Isolated on a solid flat pure green #00FF00 background, evenly lit, no shadow on the background, no ground, no text\"\n",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 720,
			"width": 560,
			"height": 360,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "krea-prop-green",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## krea-prop-green\nstyle\n# Krea 2 props to cut out: a filmed 1990s look, flat on, on pure green.\ntemplate: \"A prop for a 1995 CD-ROM full-motion-video game, photographed straight on in a flat front view for chroma-key compositing: {prompt}. Isolated on a solid flat pure green #00FF00 background, evenly lit, no shadow on the background, no ground, no people, no text\"\n",
			"x": 640,
			"y": 720,
			"width": 560,
			"height": 360,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "prop-keep",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## prop-keep\nstyle\n# Holds a prop steady in edits: only the named part changes.\ntemplate: \"Keep the exact same object, same shape, size, position, framing, materials, colours, lighting and camera quality, and the same solid flat green screen background. {prompt}\"\n",
			"x": 1280,
			"y": 720,
			"width": 560,
			"height": 300,
			"color": "5"
		}
	],
	"edges": []
}